{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>There shall not be a man's implement upon a woman.</b> Because it is disgraceful and licentiousness; therefore Yael did not take a sword or a spear, but only the hammer and the tent-peg to crush Sisera's temple. And this passage is juxtaposed here because the matter above dealt with matters of war, and a woman was created only to establish seed; and if she goes out to war she will accustom herself to harlotry — and likewise if a man wears a woman's garment."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:42.545787262Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}